WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.270
In 1866, campaigners founded
the National Secular Society.

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.670
More than a hundred and fifty years later,

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.720
it is still campaigning.

4
00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:13.680
Yet many religious people call
themselves secularists too.

5
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:18.040
And some atheists and Humanists argue
that you don't need religious rules,

6
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.440
such as prayer or fasting,
to be a good person.

7
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.530
So can a believer and an
atheist agree on how to live?

8
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.580
And where do they part ways?

9
00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.280
In this mission, you'll meet
four non-religious positions:

10
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:35.830
atheism, agnosticism,
Humanism and secularism.

11
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.820
Then you'll hear how Muslims
answer that challenge,

12
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.010
using the Qur'an and the
example of the Prophet.

13
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.780
Your mission: find out where believers
and atheists agree on how to live,

14
00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.270
and where they part ways.
